Package: smimr
Title: Stochastic Mobile-Immobile Model (SMIM) Fits to Solute Breakthrough Curves
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mitchell J.", "Liddick", email = "mliddick@nd.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Sabrina N.", "Volponi", role = "aut", comment = "author of the original MATLAB SMIMfit (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.11147719, CC BY 4.0)"),
    person("Michael J.", "Schmidt", role = "aut", comment = "author of the original SMIMfit library (github.com/mjs271/SMIMfit)"))
Description: An R port of the SMIMfit MATLAB library of Volponi (2024) and Schmidt (2020)
    for fitting the truncated-power-law Stochastic Mobile-Immobile Model of Volponi et al.
    (2025) <doi:10.1029/2024JG008225> to conservative-tracer breakthrough curves: the de Hoog
    inverse Laplace transform, the complex incomplete-gamma waiting-time transform, the
    1/C-weighted objective of the original plus a log-residual alternative, Latin-hypercube
    multi-start bounded least squares, and Jacobian-based standard errors. Numerical
    equivalence with the MATLAB original is checked by the package tests.
